# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Jayde.IO environment example — copy to `.env` for local Astro dev, and to
# `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler pages dev`. NEVER commit real values.
# In production these live in the Cloudflare Pages dashboard, not in the repo.
#
# Email delivery uses Cloudflare Email Routing via the companion Worker
# (worker-mailer/) — NO third-party email service / API key. The recipient
# (Jayde.cork@gmail.com) and sender (website@jayde.io) are set in
# worker-mailer/wrangler.toml.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── BUILD-TIME, PUBLIC (safe to expose in the browser) ───────────────────────
# Turnstile *site* key. Baked into the static contact widget at build time via
# import.meta.env.PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY. The test key below always passes and
# works on any hostname incl. localhost — replace with your real site key.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA

# ── RUNTIME, SERVER-ONLY (Cloudflare Pages Function bindings / secrets) ───────
# Read as context.env.* inside functions/api/contact.ts. Not exposed to the
# browser. Set as encrypted secrets in Pages (Production and Preview), or here in
# `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler pages dev`.

# Turnstile *secret* key (secret). Test secret below pairs with the test site key.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# Shared key between this Function and the jayde-io-mailer Worker (any long
# random string; set the SAME value on both). The Function sends it as the
# X-Mailer-Key header; the Worker refuses anything else.
MAILER_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Comma-separated hostnames the form is allowed to be submitted from, and which
# Turnstile siteverify must report. Include preview hosts as needed.
ALLOWED_HOSTNAMES=jayde.io,www.jayde.io,localhost,127.0.0.1

# The MAILER service binding (to the jayde-io-mailer Worker) is configured on the
# Pages project itself (dashboard: Settings → Functions → Service bindings), not
# as an env var here.
